#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## A mixture-of-experts layer on 32 tokens: 8 experts, each an 8 x 8
## projection adapted at rank 2, the top 2 chosen per token. How the
## tokens spread over the experts, the sparse layer against the dense
## reference, and what running only the chosen experts saves.
## Run with "just demo-lib MoE routing".

"moe:" u_se< "MoE"
"lo:" u_se< "LoRA"

u:r_ipple := { c n -> s_in c * f_loat (r_ange n) * r_ange n }
R := 8 8 r_eshape 0.9 u:r_ipple 64
ex := (8 8 8 r_eshape 0.7 u:r_ipple 512, 8 2 8 r_eshape 0.4 u:r_ipple 128, 8 8 2 r_eshape 0.3 u:r_ipple 128, 4.0 lo:s_caling 2)
x := 8 32 r_eshape 1.3 u:r_ipple 256
P := moe:s_oftmax R moe:s_cores x
G := 2 moe:t_opk P
## Each expert's share of the tokens (they sum to 2, the top 2), the
## mean entropy of the routing (log 8 = 2.08 would be no preference),
## and the load-balancing loss (1 when even).
moe:f_requency G
moe:e_ntropy P
(P, G) moe:b_alance 2
## The sparse layer equals the dense one that runs every expert (1).
0.000000000001 > 'm_ax r_/ r_avel a_bs ((ex, G) moe:c_ombine x) - (ex, G) moe:d_ense x
## Expert passes: the sparse layer runs 2 of 8 per token.
(f_loat '+ r_/ r_avel G > 0.0) c_at f_loat 8 * 32
